Embercall Industries is a corporation. [[Org/Pyrelight/index|Pyrelight]] operates under its corporate banner.

The company is small and was only founded a few months ago; no owner is named on paper, and it is held by a second, private corporation that paid to keep its own details out of reach. Its recorded headquarters is P.O. Box 9C at the [[Org/Gryphonline/index|Gryphonline]] distribution center.

Embercall made the radar dish that stood on the roof of the roller rink, now in the hands of [[Org/Iconoclasm/index|Iconoclasm]], and the signal it received appears to come from the Gryphonline distribution center as well.

It is one of a set: [[Org/Pyrelight/index|Pyrelight]] has the local gangs mount dishes like it on rooftops across the poorer districts, over places where crowds gather.

[[Aut]] says the Embercall is a derivative of the [[Voidsong]], and that [[Divinity/Ashen Pact/Pyre|Pyre]] has to do with it.

The radar dish network Tywelwyn was building is tied to [[Divinity/Ashen Pact/Pyre|Pyre]]; his notes point to the Embercall as the source of its hardware.

Embercall first appears in the newspapers a little under two years ago, some six months after the [[Voidsong]] was first heard, in the first reports of the wall of fire around [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Teller's Run/index|Teller's Run]]. Only a small part of the government's rescue parties came back out through the flame, and those who did spoke of the Embercall and died soon after. A radio communications company named Embercall Incorporated also ran a hiring notice in the listings about a year ago.

Under the Embercall name the company runs a research program on the [[Voidsong]], worked by contractors from the compound on the far side of the fracture beneath [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Teller's Run/index|Teller's Run]]. Four projects were logged there. Its works beneath Teller's Run, on the sewer side of the crack, have since been destroyed: the control system for the pumps that gathered magic there, and the hall they stood in, came down in an explosion.

Synthesis tried to build a new harmony in the Voidsong's likeness. It is marked a failure, but it produced the Embercall proper: a song that must be held into this world by a living, thinking antenna and that eats at the [[Phenomena/Firmament|firmament]] instead of passing through it, which the company counts a virtue. Hybridization grafts new properties onto the Voidsong itself and is still running, promising but expensive, burning through stored magic faster than the company can gather it. Entrainment is in planning: reach the source of the Voidsong and change what emits it, rather than the song it sends out. Dissonance is also in planning, and would turn the Voidsong back on itself until it destroys the firmament; the company calls it the likeliest to work and the hardest, needing the cooperation of many listeners.

The projects carry the names [[People/Camden Levine|Camden Levine]], [[People/Alastair Moss|Alastair Moss]], [[Org/Sable and Suns/People/Lark Crowe|Lark Crowe]] and [[People/Damien Reese|Damien Reese]]. One of the company's contractors mapped the radar dishes for himself and drew the [[Org/Iridescent Church/Convox/Inquisition/index|Inquisition]] onto the network; the dishes were scrapped, and [[Org/Pyrelight/People/The Spark|the Spark]] was told to deal with him. Funding comes through [[Org/Amber Call/People/Benjamin Grayson|Grayson]], who calls it work for the good of the pact.
